+# Browser-observation v2 Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan.
+
+**Goal:** Add an additive, fail-closed `browser_observation_v2` protocol to the isolated `codex-chatgpt-web` helper and integrate it with Ludory's upstream dev-host bridge without changing compatibility-v1 or the stable launcher.
+
+**Architecture:** The helper negotiates v2 through the existing `ready.features` frame, derives a single trace-bound observation inside the browser worker after model selection, upload-stream completion, and visible-chip checks, and emits it before the send barrier. The launcher client validates the event and holds `send_activation_ack` until the observation callback completes. Ludory keeps preflight capability separate from same-turn post-turn observation and only accepts the upstream profile for Art Acceptance.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node.js 22+ ESM, TypeScript, Bun tests/build, Playwright browser worker, Ludory JavaScript tests.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-browser-observation-v2-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Work only in this isolated upstream worktree plus the Ludory PR worktree; do not modify the installed stable launcher or stable profile.
+- Preserve compatibility-v1 wire frames and behavior. A v1 helper is unavailable for Ludory Art Acceptance, never a fallback.
+- Build and inspect the helper from the isolated DEV profile only; retain the existing descriptor trust registration.
+- Derive model, image bytes, SHA-256, byte count, upload completion, and visible attachment evidence inside the trusted browser helper. Never accept caller declarations as observations.
+- Keep the Ludory user edit `packages/studio/bin/ludory.mjs` untouched and stage files explicitly.
+- Do not claim Web/ImageGen/Release PASS without fresh evidence from the corresponding gate. Do not merge PR #13.
+
+## Task 1: Freeze the implementation surface and add the plan
+
+**Files:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-browser-observation-v2-design.md`, this plan.
+
+- Re-read the approved design and record the exact upstream/Ludory frame sequence, state transitions, limits, and error codes in the implementation notes.
+- Verify the source tree and tests named by the design exist before editing.
+- Run a static consistency check over the design and plan; do not alter unrelated docs.
+
+## Task 2: Define the shared v2 protocol types and validation tests first
+
+**Files:** `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/browser-observation.ts`, `tests/browser-observation.test.ts`.
+
+- Write failing tests for the feature identifier, strict observation schema, canonical model mapping, trace binding, attachment identity, SHA-256/size fields, upload/chip completion flags, and rejection of unknown or contradictory fields.
+- Implement the smallest shared parser/constants module. Support the generic upstream family/effort matrix, while leaving Ludory's `gpt-6-sol` + `high` policy to the consumer.
+- Run the focused Bun test and confirm the new tests are red before implementation, then green after the minimal implementation.
+
+## Task 3: Attest upload bytes and browser completion inside the worker
+
+**Files:** `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/attachment-upload.ts`, `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/browser-worker.ts`, relevant attachment/harness tests.
+
+- Add failing regression cases for the upstream image limits, filename collision before upload, missing processing completion, missing visible chip, and mismatch between the uploaded buffer and reported digest/size.
+- Clone each upload buffer once, compute SHA-256/size from that clone, and pass the same bytes to `setInputFiles`; expose only request/processing/chip completion metadata needed by v2.
+- Keep compatibility-v1 attachment behavior unchanged; apply the stricter filename collision guard and v2 evidence path only when requested.
+- After browser-confirmed model selection and completed attachment checks, build one observation for the turn's `traceId`; emit it before the send activation barrier.
+- Run the focused attachment/worker tests and the existing harness regression suite.
+
+## Task 4: Negotiate and enforce v2 in the helper protocol
+
+**Files:** `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/browser-helper-main.ts`, `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/launcher-helper-client.ts`, `tests/launcher-helper-client.test.ts`.
+
+- Add failing tests for old helpers without the feature, valid v2 event delivery, foreign/late/duplicate events, wrong trace IDs, wrong model/effort, missing attachment, SHA/size mismatch, and callback rejection/timeout.
+- Advertise `browser_observation_v2` only in the v2-capable helper ready frame and reject a required-v2 run locally before dispatch when the feature is absent.
+- Parse and validate the helper event against the prepared image bytes and current turn. Keep bounded tombstones/state so events after completion cannot be accepted or silently re-used.
+- Make `send_activated` wait for the observation callback with the approved timeout; send `send_activation_ack` only after callback success, otherwise abort and never send.
+- Run the focused launcher tests plus all existing compatibility-v1 tests.
+
+## Task 5: Integrate the upstream profile into Ludory without weakening trust
+
+**Files:** `packages/ai/src/dev-host.mjs`, `packages/ai/src/art-review.mjs`, `packages/ai/test/dev-host.test.mjs`, `packages/ai/test/art-review.test.mjs`, `packages/studio/test/art-review-cli.test.mjs`.
+
+- Add failing Ludory tests for ready-frame/profile negotiation, inspect preflight, required high Sol turn, same-trace v2 observation, source-bound receipt, old-helper blocking, wrong model, missing image, changed source, P0/P1 rework, P2-only pass, and two reworks escalating.
+- Keep safe descriptor/executable/profile validation unchanged. Add an explicit upstream profile for `ready.features`; keep the legacy profile only for existing compatibility-v1 calls.
+- Split capability preflight from post-turn observation and remove the `imageInputVerified` preflight cycle. Art Acceptance requires v2 and the same-turn observation; no compatibility-v1 fallback.
+- Normalize only validated browser observations plus the real response text into Ludory's `HOST_OBSERVED` response, with trace/model/ref/hash/size/upload binding preserved into the receipt.
+- Enforce Ludory Art Acceptance `reasoning: high`; reject Astra/Pro/instant routes and any untrusted declaration.
+- Run all affected Ludory packages and inspect receipt bytes/source binding.
+
+## Task 6: Build isolated DEV helper and execute integration smoke
+
+**Files:** isolated DEV profile artifacts and evidence files outside tracked source as appropriate; no stable launcher edits.
+
+- Install/build the upstream helper from the isolated worktree and register it through the штатный safe descriptor path.
+- Run the real browser attachment smoke with a real image and `chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol` at `high`; capture the observed model, trace ID, attachment ref/name, SHA-256, byte size, upload processing completion, visible chip, real response, and Ludory receipt path/hash.
+- Run the negative cases against the real bridge where safely possible; preserve BLOCKED diagnostics for unavailable account/session/model/browser evidence.
+- Run a separate native Codex ImageGen capability challenge and one minimal generation smoke without making CEOS manifests a Ludory dependency. If the current session cannot provide trusted capability, record the exact blocked boundary and do not fabricate output.
+
+## Task 7: Full verification, review, and handoff
+
+**Files:** test/build artifacts and evidence reports only.
+
+- Run upstream tests/build, Ludory `npm test`, `npm run check`, `node examples/core-session.mjs`, and `git diff --check` in every affected worktree.
+- Run or inspect current Windows Node 22/24 and Ubuntu CI for the published commit; link only actual workflow runs.
+- Perform an adversarial review for trust-boundary regressions, compatibility-v1 drift, late events, and receipt source binding.
+- Commit only explicit implementation/test/docs files, preserve the user-edited `packages/studio/bin/ludory.mjs`, and leave PR #13 Draft. Report remaining blockers and do not merge.
+
+## Regression Matrix
+
+The implementation is not complete until the tests cover: valid attestation; old helper without v2; missing attachment; wrong model; Sol-only effort policy in Ludory; SHA mismatch; size mismatch; incomplete upload stream; missing visible chip; filename collision; foreign/duplicate/stale/late `traceId`; callback rejection; callback timeout; preflight/post-turn separation; changed image/source; P0/P1 → `REWORK`; P2-only → `PASS_ART`; two `REWORK` → `ESCALATE`; and compatibility-v1 unchanged.
