+# Browser-observed attachment protocol v2
+
+Status: Variant A approved by the Ludory integration owner; this document is
+the revised schema-review artifact. Implementation is intentionally not
+included.
+
+## 1. Purpose and boundary
+
+The current helper already performs the security-relevant browser work:
+
+1. it selects the requested ChatGPT model family in the DOM;
+2. it passes file payloads to Playwright `setInputFiles`;
+3. it observes the upload processing stream, including
+   `file.processing.completed`;
+4. it waits for the corresponding visible attachment chip before sending.
+
+The missing boundary is export. The helper currently exports progress and
+response text, but not the model-selection or attachment facts that it just
+verified. Ludory therefore cannot distinguish browser evidence from a caller's
+declaration.
+
+This design adds one opt-in, versioned helper event:
+`browser_observation_v2`. The event is emitted only by the trusted browser
+helper after the existing browser checks have completed. It is evidence of the
+browser-side input/model boundary, not an artistic verdict.
+
+The independent Web response remains a separate acceptance input. A
+`browser_observation_v2` event alone can never produce `PASS_ART` or a release
+verdict.
+
+### In scope
+
+- feature negotiation through the existing `ready` frame;
+- a single trace-bound observation event for a browser turn;
+- helper-side SHA-256 and byte-count calculation from image buffers passed to
+  the upload mechanism;
+- browser-confirmed model-family selection and attachment completion;
+- client-side strict validation, ordering, duplicate detection, and
+  source-consistency checks;
+- compatibility with existing compatibility-v1 callers and helpers.
+
+### Out of scope
+
+- Web-to-Web v2 delegation or subagent protocol changes;
+- independent visual review, P0/P1/P2 classification, receipt policy, or
+  `PASS_ART` calculation;
+- changing the installed launcher, stable profile, trust registration, or
+  descriptor validation;
+- CEOS manifests or capability challenges as a Ludory runtime dependency;
+- publishing this change to the upstream repository.
+
+## 2. Design choice
+
+Three alternatives were considered:
+
+| Option | Description | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| A | Add an opt-in `browser_observation_v2` feature and one structured event to the existing helper protocol. | **Selected** |
+| B | Reconstruct evidence in the daemon from progress frames, prompt declarations, or upload logs. | Rejected: not browser-observed and cannot prove the visible chip or selected DOM model. |
+| C | Introduce a second side channel between the launcher and Ludory. | Rejected: expands the trust boundary and duplicates the existing helper transport. |
+
+Option A keeps the existing line protocol, makes support explicit, and lets
+old callers continue unchanged. The new event is suppressed unless the
+caller explicitly requires v2, so a compatibility-v1 consumer never receives
+an unknown event merely because it is talking to a newer helper.
+
+## 3. Negotiation and compatibility
+
+The helper advertises support in its existing ready frame:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "ready",
+  "features": [
+    "progress",
+    "tool-boundary-ack",
+    "completion-fence",
+    "multipart-stage-ack",
+    "skill-attachments",
+    "browser_observation_v2"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+The feature name is the version identifier. It is not inferred from the
+helper version, package version, executable path, or a declaration from the
+caller.
+
+`BrowserTurn` gains an optional `requireBrowserObservationV2` flag and an
+optional `onBrowserObservationV2` callback. The launcher client behaves as
+follows:
+
+1. it starts the helper and waits for `ready`;
+2. when `requireBrowserObservationV2` is true, it requires the exact
+   `browser_observation_v2` feature before writing the `run` frame;
+3. if the feature is absent, it rejects locally with
+   `browser_observation_v2_unavailable` and does not dispatch the turn;
+4. if the flag is false or omitted, it preserves the compatibility-v1 path and
+   does not request or expect the new event.
+
+The run frame carries the requirement explicitly:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "run",
+  "id": "turn_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
+  "turn": {
+    "traceId": "turn_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
+    "modelId": "gpt-5.6-sol",
+    "modelFamily": "6",
+    "reasoning": "high",
+    "requireBrowserObservationV2": true
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The incoming `modelId` is the existing internal transport identity. It is not
+accepted as evidence. The helper must derive the observed canonical model
+from the browser-confirmed family and selected mode described below.
+
+An old helper does not advertise the feature and cannot claim v2 support. An
+old caller never sets the requirement and remains compatible with the old
+event set. A new caller talking to an old helper is `BLOCKED`/unavailable for
+Ludory art acceptance; it must not fall back to v1.
+
+## 4. Ludory dev-host integration
+
+`BrowserDevHost` is a separate consumer of the helper line protocol. Its
+current implementation is not wire-compatible with upstream 6.1.14 by
+declaration alone: the legacy path expects a `ready` frame with
+`protocolVersion: 1`, a `capabilities` probe, `image_attached` plus a
+caller-supplied `hostObservation`, and a result that repeats that observation.
+Upstream 6.1.14 instead exposes `ready.features`, `inspect`, `prepared_selected`,
+`browser_observation_v2`, `send_activated`, `submitted`, and a text-only
+`result`. The integration must therefore use an explicit consumer-side bridge
+with two negotiated wire profiles.
+
+### Profile selection
+
+The bridge keeps compatibility-v1 unchanged for existing callers:
+
+```text
+ready.protocolVersion === 1       -> legacy profile
+ready.features is an array        -> upstream profile
+otherwise                         -> DEV_HELPER_PROTOCOL_UNSUPPORTED
+```
+
+The bridge never selects a profile from an executable name, package version,
+or a user-provided declaration. For an art-review turn, only the upstream
+profile is eligible and the exact `browser_observation_v2` feature is required.
+A legacy helper, even if it returns a field called `hostObservation`, is
+`DEV_BROWSER_OBSERVATION_V2_UNAVAILABLE` for art acceptance.
+
+### Upstream profile sequence
+
+The exact Ludory-to-upstream sequence is:
+
+```text
+discoverDevHost()
+  -> safe descriptor/profile/helper registration
+  -> spawn descriptor.helper.executable with descriptor.helper.script
+  -> upstream ready(features)
+  -> inspect(detectCapabilities=true)
+  -> run(requireBrowserObservationV2=true)
+  -> prepared_selected
+  -> prepared_selected_ack(images as data URLs)
+  -> browser_observation_v2
+  -> validate observation and invoke observation callback
+  -> send_activated
+  -> await unfinished observation callback (bounded)
+  -> send_activation_ack
+  -> submitted
+  -> result(text)
+  -> normalize validated observation + text for Ludory
+```
+
+The upstream `inspect` request is the capability preflight. It is not model or
+attachment evidence. The selected model and input evidence come only from the
+v2 event in the same run.
+
+The upstream maintenance response has a precise, limited shape. For
+`inspect(detectCapabilities=true)`, the helper writes:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "result",
+  "id": "<inspectId>",
+  "value": {
+    "authenticated": true,
+    "newChat": true,
+    "url": "<current ChatGPT URL>",
+    "solAvailable": true,
+    "extraHighAvailable": false,
+    "proAvailable": false
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`authenticated`, `newChat`, and `url` are always present. The three account
+capability booleans are present when capability detection is requested and are
+absent when `detectCapabilities=false`. `inspect.result.value` contains no
+selected model, effort, attachment, upload request, hash, chip, trace-bound
+observation, or `localToolsEnabled` field. The bridge owns
+`localToolsEnabled:false` in the v2 run configuration; it is not inspect
+evidence.
+
+Ludory keeps two disjoint records. The **preflight capability** is derived
+only from `ready.features` and the validated `inspect.result.value`; it may
+prove that the web route, account Sol capability, and v2 feature are
+available. It must not contain or require `imageInputVerified`,
+`imageInputObserved`, or `HOST_OBSERVED`. The **post-turn observation** is
+created only from the same-turn `browser_observation_v2` event after helper
+and client validation, callback success, `submitted`, and a valid result.
+
+The bridge exposes the split to the existing Ludory host with distinct
+fields:
+
+```json
+{
+  "preflight": {
+    "available": true,
+    "routeAvailable": "web-dev",
+    "modelRouteAvailable": "chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol",
+    "browserObservationV2Available": true,
+    "reasoningRequired": "high",
+    "inspect": {
+      "authenticated": true,
+      "newChat": true,
+      "url": "<current ChatGPT URL>",
+      "solAvailable": true,
+      "extraHighAvailable": false,
+      "proAvailable": false
+    }
+  },
+  "postTurn": {
+    "status": "HOST_OBSERVED",
+    "routeObserved": "web-dev",
+    "modelObserved": "gpt-6-sol",
+    "reasoningObserved": "high",
+    "imageInputObserved": true,
+    "observation": "<validated browser_observation_v2>"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`preflight` has no `modelObserved`, `imageInputVerified`,
+`imageInputObserved`, or `HOST_OBSERVED` field. `postTurn` exists only after
+the required event and result have been validated; it is the only source from
+which the compatibility response and receipt may obtain observed model or
+attachment facts.
+
+Accordingly, `planArtReview` gates attemptability on preflight availability,
+the v2 feature, the fixed Ludory route, and the art effort policy; it never
+reads `imageInputVerified` from a probe. `executeArtReview` uses the probe
+only as a preflight check and gates `HOST_OBSERVED`, the visual verdict, and
+the receipt on the same-turn post-turn observation. A missing post-turn
+observation is `BLOCKED`, not a failed preflight and not a reason to retry via
+v1. `imageInputVerified` is a post-turn result field, if retained for the
+existing Ludory response shape; it is never a preflight prerequisite.
+
+The upstream `run` frame must contain the configuration fields required by
+`browser-helper-main.ts`; the bridge must retain the validated descriptor path
+so it can send the same isolated path, not reconstruct or substitute one:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "run",
+  "id": "<traceId>",
+  "config": {
+    "appName": "ludory-web-art-review",
+    "browserHostDescriptorPath": "<validated-dev-descriptor>",
+    "turnTimeoutMs": 1800000,
+    "autoApproveToolCalls": false
+  },
+  "turn": {
+    "traceId": "<traceId>",
+    "modelId": "gpt-5.6-sol",
+    "modelFamily": "6",
+    "reasoning": "high",
+    "capabilities": {
+      "localToolsEnabled": false,
+      "solAvailable": true,
+      "extraHighAvailable": false,
+      "proAvailable": false
+    },
+    "requireBrowserObservationV2": true
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The capability values in this frame are copied from the validated upstream
+`inspect` result and are used to configure selection; they are not promoted to
+the final receipt. A v2-required art turn must use the fixed Sol route and
+`reasoning:"high"`, regardless of whether the account also exposes Pro. This
+is a Ludory Art Acceptance policy; it does not change the upstream model
+matrix. Generic upstream v2 turns retain the existing supported Sol efforts.
+
+The bridge sends the upstream `prepared_selected_ack` only with the prepared
+prompt and image data URLs derived from the source bytes already validated by
+Ludory. It does not send `hostObservation`, `imageSha256`, or any other
+attestation field as a request-side declaration.
+
+When the v2 event is valid, the bridge may project it into Ludory's existing
+response shape for compatibility, but the projection is created locally from
+the validated event and never read from `result`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "status": "HOST_OBSERVED",
+  "routeObserved": "web-dev",
+  "modelObserved": "gpt-6-sol",
+  "imageInputObserved": true,
+  "imageRef": "<observation.attachments[0].ref>",
+  "imageSha256": "<observation.attachments[0].sha256>",
+  "hostObservation": {
+    "protocolVersion": 2,
+    "source": "browser-ui",
+    "traceId": "<observation.traceId>",
+    "selectedModel": "gpt-6-sol",
+    "reasoning": "<observation.model.effort>",
+    "image": {
+      "ref": "<attachment.ref>",
+      "sha256": "<attachment.sha256>",
+      "bytes": "<attachment.bytes>"
+    },
+    "upload": {
+      "creationRequestObserved": true,
+      "processingRequestObserved": true,
+      "processingRequestKind": "<validated observation.upload.processingRequestKind>",
+      "processingEvent": "file.processing.completed",
+      "processingCompleted": true,
+      "visibleAttachmentChip": true
+    }
+  },
+  "text": "<upstream result.text>"
+}
+```
+
+`HOST_OBSERVED` is allowed only after the event has passed all checks below,
+the observation callback has completed successfully, `submitted` has arrived,
+and the result text is valid. A legacy result or an upstream text result
+without a validated event remains `BLOCKED`; no result field can manufacture
+the missing observation.
+
+### Activation acknowledgement barrier
+
+The v2 bridge uses one fixed finite callback deadline,
+`BROWSER_OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000`. The deadline starts when
+`send_activated` arrives while the observation callback promise is still
+unsettled. If the callback has already resolved, no wait is needed. The
+upstream acknowledgement is the gate that releases the browser's Send
+boundary, so no Send may occur while this wait is in progress.
+
+For an upstream v2-required pending turn, `send_activation_ack` is sent only
+from the following state transition:
+
+```text
+AWAIT_ACTIVATED
+  -- valid browser_observation_v2 --> OBSERVATION_VALIDATING
+  -- callback starts --> OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_PENDING
+  -- callback resolves before send_activated --> OBSERVATION_VALIDATED
+  -- send_activated while OBSERVATION_VALIDATED --> ACTIVATION_ACK_PENDING
+  -- send_activated while OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_PENDING --> OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_WAIT
+  -- callback resolves before the deadline --> ACTIVATION_ACK_PENDING
+  -- write succeeds --> AWAIT_SUBMITTED
+  -- callback rejects or deadline expires --> FAILED_NO_SEND
+```
+
+The bridge must not write `send_activation_ack` while the event is absent,
+malformed, mismatched, duplicated, stale, or while the observation callback is
+rejected. If `send_activated` arrives while the callback is pending, the
+bridge awaits that exact callback up to the fixed deadline. A successful
+resolution is the only transition that permits `send_activation_ack`. A
+rejection or timeout aborts and closes the turn without ACK and therefore
+without Send. If `send_activated` arrives before any valid observation, the
+bridge aborts immediately with the same no-ACK/no-Send rule. This is an
+explicit invariant, not a timing expectation.
+
+Implementation invariant: the only code path allowed to write
+`{ type: "send_activation_ack", id }` for an upstream v2 turn is guarded by
+`pending.observationState === "OBSERVATION_VALIDATED"` and a successfully
+settled `pending.observationCallback` promise. The `send_activated` handler
+may await that promise through the bounded deadline; its rejection and
+timeout paths may only abort. No fallback branch, timeout handler, or legacy
+`image_attached` branch may write that frame for a v2 turn.
+
+For compatibility-v1 turns, the existing acknowledgement behavior remains
+unchanged. That path cannot be used to grant Ludory art acceptance.
+
+## 5. Versioned wire schema
+
+The new frame is an existing `event` envelope with a versioned observation
+payload:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "event",
+  "id": "turn_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
+  "event": "browser_observation_v2",
+  "observation": {
+    "version": 2,
+    "traceId": "turn_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
+    "source": "chatgpt-web-browser",
+    "model": {
+      "canonicalId": "chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol",
+      "backendModelId": "gpt-5.6-sol",
+      "family": "6",
+      "effort": "high",
+      "selectionLabel": "High"
+    },
+    "attachments": [
+      {
+        "ref": "hero-expression",
+        "name": "hero-expression.png",
+        "mimeType": "image/png",
+        "sha256": "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
+        "bytes": 12345,
+        "upload": {
+          "creationRequestObserved": true,
+          "processingRequestObserved": true,
+          "processingRequestKind": "process_upload_stream",
+          "processingEvent": "file.processing.completed",
+          "processingCompleted": true,
+          "visibleAttachmentChip": true
+        }
+      }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Field contract
+
+| Field | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `type` | Literal `"event"`. |
+| `id` | The active helper turn id; it must equal `turn.traceId`. |
+| `event` | Literal `"browser_observation_v2"`. |
+| `observation.version` | Literal number `2`. |
+| `observation.traceId` | Exact active `traceId`; no cross-turn reuse. |
+| `observation.source` | Literal `"chatgpt-web-browser"`; identifies the trusted producer, not a caller claim. |
+| `model.canonicalId` | Canonical route derived from the browser-confirmed family and effort. Ludory art acceptance requires exact `"chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol"`. |
+| `model.backendModelId` | Exact current internal route `"gpt-5.6-sol"`; included to make the canonical-to-transport mapping explicit. |
+| `model.family` | Literal `"6"`, obtained only after browser model-family assertion. |
+| `model.effort` | Normalized selected effort: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, or `max`; the generic upstream Sol matrix remains unchanged, while Ludory Art Acceptance requires exactly `high`. |
+| `model.selectionLabel` | Non-empty label read from the selected browser control after selection confirmation. |
+| `attachments` | One or more image attachments; no skill/text files are attested by this event. |
+| `attachment.ref` | Exact prepared-image reference; unique within the observation. |
+| `attachment.name` | Exact file name passed to the upload mechanism; unique across the complete upload file list, including image and skill files. |
+| `attachment.mimeType` | Lower-case `image/*` MIME type from the prepared image payload. |
+| `attachment.sha256` | Lower-case 64-hex SHA-256 of the exact image buffer passed to `setInputFiles`. |
+| `attachment.bytes` | Positive safe integer equal to the exact image buffer byte length. |
+| `upload.creationRequestObserved` | Literal `true`; the helper matched the file's owned `POST /backend-api/files` request. |
+| `upload.processingRequestObserved` | Literal `true`; the helper matched the same file's owned processing request. |
+| `upload.processingRequestKind` | `process_upload_stream` or `claim_and_finish`, matching the current upstream observer's supported endpoint. |
+| `upload.processingEvent` | Literal `"file.processing.completed"`, observed in the owned upload-processing stream. |
+| `upload.processingCompleted` | Literal `true`; no earlier or inferred upload state is accepted. |
+| `upload.visibleAttachmentChip` | Literal `true`; set only after the corresponding named chip/group is visible in the composer. |
+
+The schema intentionally does not export a server `file_id`. It is not needed
+for Ludory source binding, may be unstable across retries, and would add a
+server identifier to a local evidence contract. The stable source identity is
+`ref` plus the helper-computed hash and byte count.
+
+Before the upload observer or `setInputFiles` is touched, the helper builds
+the complete upstream file list returned by `chatGptPromptFilePayloads`:
+all image files followed by all skill files. Every upload name must be
+non-empty and unique in that complete list. An exact image/image,
+skill/skill, or image/skill name collision is rejected before any upload
+request can be created; there is no partial upload and no v2 observation.
+The check covers the actual generated image names (`<ref>.<extension>`) and
+the validated skill-file names, not only the names later exported in
+`observation.attachments`.
+
+The observation does not introduce a second attachment limit. It inherits the
+upstream limits enforced by `chatGptPromptFilePayloads`:
+
+- at most 10 total attachments per message, counting image files and skill
+  text files together;
+- each image is non-empty and at most 20,000,000 bytes;
+- all image and skill-file buffers together are at most 50,000,000 bytes;
+- the v2 `attachments` array contains only image files, so its maximum is
+  `10 - skillFiles.length` for the prepared prompt.
+
+The v2 bridge adopts these upstream limits; it must not introduce a hidden
+10 MiB ceiling. The current Ludory `MAX_INPUT_IMAGE_BYTES` value is a legacy
+consumer guard and must not be presented as the upstream protocol limit. If a
+separate Ludory product policy retains a stricter preflight, that rejection is
+explicitly local and blocked, never evidence that the upload occurred.
+
+## 6. What the helper is allowed to attest
+
+The event is produced inside `ChatGptBrowserWorker` only after all of the
+following facts are true for the same turn:
+
+### Model
+
+`selectModelAndEffort` has selected the requested family and has completed the
+existing browser assertions, including the model-family announcement,
+effort slider state, selected control label, and final post-menu confirmation.
+For the accepted route the helper constructs the canonical route from the
+confirmed family and effort, not from the incoming backend id alone:
+
+```text
+family 6 + low              -> chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol-instant
+family 6 + medium/high/xhigh -> chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol
+family 6 + max              -> chatgpt-web/gpt-6-pro (Astra/Pro)
+```
+
+For Ludory Web Art Acceptance, the exact canonical id must be
+`chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol` and the dispatched and observed effort must be exactly
+`high`. The generic upstream v2 matrix still admits `medium`, `high`, and
+`xhigh`; `medium` and `xhigh` are rejected only by the Ludory art-specific
+policy as `browser_observation_v2_art_effort_mismatch`. `low` is GPT-6 Sol
+Instant, and `max` is the GPT-6 Pro/Astra route; neither may be attested as
+GPT-6 Sol. A family-5.6 or Luna selection also fails the Ludory gate.
+
+### Image bytes
+
+The worker builds image payloads from the prepared prompt and, immediately
+before `input.setInputFiles(files)`, computes SHA-256 and byte length from each
+image `Buffer` in the exact object passed to Playwright. The implementation
+must not hash a path, data URL string, declaration, or server response.
+
+The helper records the image `ref`, file name, MIME type, hash, byte count, and
+the exact source `Buffer` in an in-memory per-turn record. The record also
+contains the matched creation request id, processing request id, observed file
+id when present, and the chip locator key. These request ids are helper-local
+correlation data; they are not accepted from the caller and are not used as a
+portable receipt identity. The record is discarded with the turn and is never
+reused for another `traceId`.
+
+### Upload and visible attachment
+
+The existing upload observer is started before `setInputFiles`. The worker
+must clone each source buffer once, compute the hash and byte count from that
+clone, and pass that same clone in the `setInputFiles` payload. For every
+attested image, the helper must correlate all of the following to the same
+per-turn record, exact file name/ref, and upload request ids:
+
+- the owned creation request for that file;
+- the owned upload-processing request for that file;
+- the processing stream's file id when the server supplies one;
+- the complete stream termination with
+  `file.processing.completed`;
+- no processing error, failure, cancellation, or incomplete stream;
+- the named attachment group/chip for that exact file visible in the same
+  composer;
+- the Send control enabled after attachment readiness.
+
+The event is emitted after these checks and before the send-activation
+boundary. A file id, a successful creation request, a visible loading card, or
+an enabled Send button by itself is insufficient. A processing completion for
+another file, another request, or another trace is not evidence for this
+attachment.
+
+## 7. Turn state and event ordering
+
+The v2-required path has this state machine:
+
+```text
+READY
+  -> NEGOTIATED
+  -> RUN_ACCEPTED
+  -> PROMPT_SELECTED
+  -> MODEL_CONFIRMED
+  -> ATTACHMENT_OBSERVING
+  -> ATTACHMENT_CONFIRMED
+  -> OBSERVATION_VALIDATING
+  -> OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_PENDING
+  -> OBSERVATION_VALIDATED
+  -> SEND_ACTIVATED
+  -> ACTIVATION_ACK_PENDING
+  -> SUBMITTED
+  -> RESPONSE
+  -> COMPLETE
+```
+
+Failure from any state is terminal for that turn. A required observation is not
+optional and cannot be added after the answer has started.
+
+`send_activated` is a barrier, not a permission to bypass an unfinished
+callback. If it arrives in `OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_PENDING`, the turn enters
+`OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_WAIT` and waits at most
+`BROWSER_OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS`; successful resolution proceeds to
+`ACTIVATION_ACK_PENDING`, while rejection or timeout enters `FAILED_NO_SEND`.
+The latter is terminal and records a tombstone before abort/cleanup, so a
+callback that resolves later cannot release Send or produce evidence.
+
+The client enforces these rules:
+
+- `browser_observation_v2` must have a pending turn with the same `id`;
+- `observation.traceId` must equal both `id` and `turn.traceId`;
+- it must be the first and only v2 observation for that turn;
+- it must arrive after prompt selection and before `send_activated`,
+  `submitted`, or `result`;
+- it must contain exactly the prepared image set after strict identity
+  comparison; extra, missing, duplicate, or reordered identities are rejected;
+- its model and attachment facts must pass all value and consistency checks;
+- `result` for a v2-required turn without a valid observation is rejected as
+  `browser_observation_v2_missing`;
+- `send_activated` is accepted only after observation validation and successful
+  completion of the consumer callback; if that callback is unresolved, the
+  client waits up to `BROWSER_OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS`, then aborts on
+  rejection or timeout and writes no `send_activation_ack`;
+- a late, foreign, duplicate, or contradictory v2 frame is a protocol error
+  and fails closed. It must not be ignored as ordinary progress.
+
+The helper also keeps a per-run observation state. It cannot emit the event
+twice, emit it for a turn without a required image, or emit it after the
+submission callback. This protects the producer side even when the consumer
+is not the reference client.
+
+### Late and post-completion frames
+
+The consumer keeps bounded terminal tombstones for completed and failed
+`traceId`s for at least the configured turn timeout. If a
+`browser_observation_v2` frame arrives after `result`, `error`, abort, timeout,
+or helper-side cleanup, the bridge classifies it as
+`browser_observation_v2_stale`, rejects the turn if still possible, closes the
+helper connection, and discards the frame. It never attaches late evidence to
+a new turn or to an existing receipt.
+
+An observation with an id that is neither active nor present in the bounded
+tombstones is a foreign trace and fails as
+`browser_observation_v2_trace_mismatch`. Ordinary legacy frames retain their
+compatibility-v1 handling, but a v2 observation is never silently ignored.
+After the helper is closed, all queued late frames and late callback
+resolutions are discarded; the corresponding Ludory operation remains
+`BLOCKED`.
+
+## 8. Client-facing API
+
+The existing `LauncherBrowserHelperClient.run()` continues to resolve to the
+response text. The additive `BrowserTurn` fields are:
+
+```ts
+requireBrowserObservationV2?: boolean;
+onBrowserObservationV2?: (
+  observation: BrowserObservationV2,
+) => void | Promise<void>;
+```
+
+For a required turn, the client:
+
+1. performs feature negotiation before dispatch;
+2. parses and validates the event rather than constructing one;
+3. compares the observed image identity, SHA-256, and byte count with the
+   prepared image bytes as an independent consistency check;
+4. invokes `onBrowserObservationV2` with the validated helper evidence;
+5. if `send_activated` arrives while that callback is unsettled, waits for its
+   result for at most `BROWSER_OBSERVATION_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS`;
+6. aborts the browser turn without ACK/Send if the callback rejects or times
+   out;
+7. rejects the final result if the callback was never delivered a valid event.
+
+The client-side comparison is not a replacement for helper evidence. It only
+detects a mismatch between the helper's attestation and the prepared bytes
+known by the daemon. The browser-observed flags remain meaningful only because
+the event came from a helper that passed the negotiated feature boundary and
+performed the DOM/network checks internally.
+
+Ludory's adapter must request v2 for art acceptance and persist the validated
+observation alongside the independent Web response. It must enforce its own
+policy:
+
+- no observation or no real Web response: `BLOCKED`;
+- P0/P1: `REWORK`;
+- P2-only with a real independent visual verdict: `PASS_ART`;
+- two `REWORK` results in one run: `ESCALATE`.
+
+No code in this helper may turn the observation into a visual verdict.
+
+## 9. Failure codes and handling
+
+The helper uses the existing error envelope. v2-specific errors use stable
+codes; local protocol validation errors use the same code names without
+pretending that the browser produced evidence.
+
+| Code | Boundary | Required action |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `browser_observation_v2_unavailable` | `ready` did not advertise v2. | Reject before dispatch; Ludory remains `BLOCKED`. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_required` | Required flag was requested but the helper cannot satisfy it. | Fail the turn; never fall back to v1. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_attachment_missing` | No prepared image exists for a required art turn. | Fail before send. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_attachment_incomplete` | Processing completion, visible chip, or Send readiness was not confirmed. | Fail before send; no observation. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_model_mismatch` | Browser-confirmed canonical route is not `chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol`, or the effort is not `medium`, `high`, or `xhigh`. | Fail before send; no observation. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_art_effort_mismatch` | A Ludory Art Acceptance turn observes a Sol effort other than `high`. | Abort before ACK/Send; no art receipt. The generic upstream Sol matrix is unchanged. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_hash_mismatch` | Helper evidence differs from prepared image bytes. | Abort and reject; no receipt. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_upload_mismatch` | File name/ref, creation request, processing request, file id, or visible chip does not match the source-buffer record. | Abort and reject; no observation. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_file_name_collision` | Two names in the complete image-plus-skill upload list are equal. | Reject before `setInputFiles`; no upload request, observation, or receipt. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_trace_mismatch` | `id`, `traceId`, or prepared-turn identity differs. | Protocol failure; terminate the helper connection if needed. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_duplicate` | More than one observation for one trace. | Protocol failure; no evidence is accepted. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_stale` | Observation arrives after submission/result or after the pending turn is gone. | Protocol failure; no evidence is accepted. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_callback_failed` | The consumer observation callback rejected. | Abort without `send_activation_ack`; no Send or receipt. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_callback_timeout` | `send_activated` arrived while the observation callback remained unsettled past the fixed deadline. | Abort without `send_activation_ack`; no Send or receipt. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_invalid` | Schema, bounds, MIME, hash, or field invariant is invalid. | Protocol failure; fail closed. |
+| `browser_observation_v2_missing` | Required turn reached result without a valid observation. | Reject the result; Ludory remains `BLOCKED`. |
+
+The current helper's generic `error` frame remains valid for compatibility.
+The new implementation should use the structured existing envelope when a
+v2-specific error originates in the worker and preserve the existing status,
+error type, and retryability semantics.
+
+## 10. Producer integration points
+
+The smallest implementation surface is:
+
+1. `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/browser-worker.ts`
+   - add the optional `BrowserTurn` requirement/callback;
+   - return attachment observation metadata from the existing attachment
+     stage without weakening its current checks;
+   - compute hashes from the `Buffer` objects passed to `setInputFiles`;
+   - construct and emit the observation only after model and attachment
+     confirmation, before send activation.
+2. `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/attachment-upload.ts`
+   - retain the current stream/error behavior;
+   - expose only the minimal completion metadata needed to bind each expected
+     file name to `file.processing.completed`.
+3. `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/browser-helper-main.ts`
+   - advertise the feature;
+   - validate `requireBrowserObservationV2`;
+   - forward the worker callback as the versioned event with the same `id`.
+4. `src/adapters/chatgpt-web/launcher-helper-client.ts`
+   - parse the new event;
+   - negotiate the feature before dispatch;
+   - validate correlation, ordering, duplicate/stale behavior, and hashes;
+   - invoke the additive callback while preserving the text return type.
+
+No launcher binary, installed runtime, stable profile, or descriptor trust
+check is modified by this protocol extension.
+
+## 11. Regression coverage
+
+The upstream test suite must cover the following matrix:
+
+| Test | Expected result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Ready frame advertises v2 and a valid required turn | Observation reaches the callback with the exact trace id, model, hashes, sizes, and upload flags. |
+| Compatibility-v1 helper with no v2 feature | A v2-required client rejects before dispatch; an ordinary v1 turn still works. |
+| Required turn with no image | `browser_observation_v2_attachment_missing`; no Send/submit boundary. |
+| GPT-6 Sol `medium`, `high`, and `xhigh` | Canonical `chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol` is admissible; the actual selected effort is retained. |
+| Ludory Art Acceptance with `medium` or `xhigh` | Generic upstream v2 remains compatible with the unchanged model matrix, but the Ludory art policy rejects the turn as `browser_observation_v2_art_effort_mismatch`; only `reasoning:"high"` is dispatched for this path. |
+| GPT-6 `low` / Sol Instant | No GPT-6 Sol attestation; `browser_observation_v2_model_mismatch`. |
+| GPT-6 `max` / Astra-Pro | No GPT-6 Sol attestation; `browser_observation_v2_model_mismatch`. |
+| GPT-5.6 family or Luna | No observation for Ludory art acceptance; `browser_observation_v2_model_mismatch`. |
+| Upload processing stream without completion | No observation; `browser_observation_v2_attachment_incomplete`. |
+| Visible chip before processing completion | No observation; processing completion is still required. |
+| Creation request belongs to another file/trace | No observation; `browser_observation_v2_upload_mismatch`. |
+| Processing request/file id belongs to another file | No observation; `browser_observation_v2_upload_mismatch`. |
+| Source buffer mutated between hash and `setInputFiles` | Hash is computed from the cloned buffer passed to upload; any mismatch fails closed. |
+| Wrong file name/ref chip becomes visible | No observation; `browser_observation_v2_upload_mismatch`. |
+| Duplicate image names, duplicate skill names, or image/skill filename collision in the complete upload list | Rejected before `setInputFiles` with `browser_observation_v2_file_name_collision`; no upload request or observation. |
+| More than 10 total upstream attachments, image over 20,000,000 bytes, or total over 50,000,000 bytes | Upstream admission fails; no v2 event or receipt. |
+| Ludory's conservative 10 MiB outer image gate | `DEV_IMAGE_INPUT_INVALID`/blocked before dispatch; no claim that the upstream event occurred. |
+| Hash mismatch | Client rejects the event and aborts; no result is accepted. |
+| Byte-count mismatch | Client rejects the event and aborts. |
+| Foreign `id` or mismatched `observation.traceId` | Protocol failure; no callback. |
+| Duplicate observation for one turn | Protocol failure; first event is not promoted to a completed receipt. |
+| `send_activated` before observation validation | No `send_activation_ack`; turn is aborted. |
+| Observation callback pending at `send_activated`, then resolves before the 10-second deadline | ACK is sent only after resolution; the helper may proceed to `submitted`. |
+| Observation callback rejects at `send_activated` | No `send_activation_ack`, no Send, and `browser_observation_v2_callback_failed`. |
+| Observation callback remains pending past the 10-second deadline | No `send_activation_ack`, no Send, and `browser_observation_v2_callback_timeout`. |
+| Stale observation after `submitted`, `result`, abort, or timeout | Tombstone catches it; helper connection closes and no evidence is accepted. |
+| Unknown post-completion observation id | Foreign trace failure; no evidence is accepted. |
+| Extra/missing/duplicate attachment refs | Protocol failure; no evidence accepted. |
+| Upstream `ready` has no v2 feature | Ludory returns `DEV_BROWSER_OBSERVATION_V2_UNAVAILABLE`; no v1 fallback. |
+| Upstream `inspect` reports route availability but no turn observation | Capability remains preflight-only; final status is `BLOCKED`. |
+| Text response without a v2 event | Required turn rejects as missing; v1 turn remains compatible. |
+| v2 event without the explicit requirement | Helper does not emit it; v1 event stream remains unchanged. |
+| Independent Web response is absent or not visual | Ludory remains `BLOCKED`; observation alone cannot become `PASS_ART`. |
+| Real visual verdict with only P2 findings | `PASS_ART` is eligible, subject to source-bound receipt checks. |
+| Any P0/P1 finding | `REWORK`; no `PASS_ART`. |
+| Second `REWORK` in one run | `ESCALATE`; no third automatic acceptance attempt. |
+| Source artifact changes before callback/result or receipt | Source revalidation fails; no receipt is written. |
+
+Use the existing helper-process fixture in
+`tests/launcher-helper-client.test.ts` for wire negotiation and correlation,
+the attachment fixtures in `tests/attachment-upload.test.ts` for completion
+semantics, and browser-worker contract fixtures for model/chip ordering. No
+test may mark a synthetic event as `HOST_OBSERVED`; test fixtures must remain
+clearly separate from real smoke evidence.
+
+## 12. Isolated DEV build and smoke plan
+
+The implementation will be built only in the upstream checkout:
+
+```text
+bun install --frozen-lockfile
+bun run scripts/build-browser-helper.ts .launcher-runtime/browser-helper.cjs
+```
+
+The supported DEV harness then uses the working-tree helper through the
+isolated DEV launcher/profile:
+
+```text
+bun run dev:launcher
+bun run src/cli.ts dev status
+bun run dev:chat <name> --model chatgpt-web/gpt-6-sol <message>
+```
+
+The exact smoke command may be a bounded helper/client fixture if the named
+DEV chat command does not expose the new callback. It must still use the real
+browser surface and the isolated profile. The smoke evidence must record:
+
+- the helper build path and source commit;
+- `ready.features` containing `browser_observation_v2`;
+- the requested and observed canonical model;
+- the actual test-image path, byte count, and independently calculated SHA-256;
+- the helper observation's byte count and SHA-256;
+- `file.processing.completed` and visible attachment-chip confirmation;
+- the real Web answer and its independent visual verdict;
+- the resulting source-bound Ludory receipt path.
+
+If any of these is unavailable, the run remains `BLOCKED` at that exact
+boundary. A unit-test event, a prompt declaration, a launcher setting, or a
+stale capability marker is not a substitute for the missing observation.
+
+### Separate ImageGen smoke
+
+ImageGen is tested independently through the native Codex `image_gen` tool. It
+is not a helper protocol requirement, and Ludory must not import, read, or
+require a CEOS manifest to execute its own workflows. The smoke has four
+separate outcomes:
+
+1. `IMAGEGEN_UNAVAILABLE`: the native ImageGen capability is not exposed in
+   the current Codex session;
+2. `IMAGEGEN_ROUTING_ERROR`: the capability is exposed and challenged, but the
+   actual native call fails at routing or generation;
+3. `IMAGEGEN_CAPABILITY_CHALLENGE_BLOCKED`: the run-scoped capability
+   challenge itself is unavailable or rejects the legacy/old capability
+   handshake;
+4. `BLOCKED_SESSION_CONTEXT_UNVERIFIED`: the current Codex context is not
+   trusted, so generation must not be attempted.
+
+Only after a fresh current-turn, run-scoped capability challenge succeeds may
+the native ImageGen call be made. The smoke records the actual tool result or
+the exact failure boundary; it never uses a CEOS manifest, environment flag,
+stale marker, synthetic PNG, or declaration to turn a blocked result into
+ImageGen PASS.
+
+## 13. Security and release gates
+
+- The helper remains the sole producer of browser-observed claims.
+- The caller cannot set `browserObserved`, processing completion, chip
+  visibility, hash, or byte count through the run message.
+- The stable launcher registration and `DEV_DESCRIPTOR_UNTRUSTED` boundary are
+  untouched.
+- A v2 absence is a hard boundary for Ludory art acceptance, not a reason to
+  downgrade to v1.
+- Web visual evaluation and browser input attestation are separate evidence
+  classes.
+- The Ludory PR remains Draft and is not merged until the real Web E2E, the
+  separate ImageGen smoke, and the required current CI checks have fresh
+  evidence.
+
+This document is ready for schema review. Implementation should begin only
+after the exact event names and field contracts above are approved.
